      "category": "Text",
      "text": "602. All signatures to a petition must be duly acknowledged before a notary. Individual acknowledgments may be taken or a subscribing witness may witness and acknowledge the signatures of one or more petitioners. In the case of corporate petitioners, the corporate name shall be signed by an officer thereunto duly authorized, the corporate seal shall be affixed and a corporate form of acknowledgment executed.",
